WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.370
Deadpool 2 is a cinematic blessing the likes
of which the world hasn't seen since Infinity

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:06.940
War came out two weeks earlier.

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:11.900
That said, the sarcastic, fourth-wall-breaking
X-Men spinoff is up there with the very best

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:16.560
of superhero sequels - like Spider-Man 2,
X2, or the second Godfather.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:20.720
It raises the stakes, widens the world, and
racks up a bone-crunching body count.

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.910
The movie's got everything you need but a
free chimichanga.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:28.449
Were you too busy laughing to catch exactly
what was going on at the end of Deadpool 2?

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:29.939
If so, don't worry.

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:34.170
We've got ourselves a cell-phone-quality camera
rip of this R-rated blockbuster, and we've

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.590
combed through it frame-by-frame to get you
all the facts you need.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:42.000
So buckle up, family - it's time to break
down the insane ending of Deadpool 2.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:44.480
Token of affection

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.200
After seeing Deadpool give up his life for
Russell, Cable is forced to reconsider his

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:49.720
values.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.960
Thanks to Back to the Future-style time travel
causality waves, he can see that Deadpool

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.360
and Company's efforts to save Russell's soul
were ultimately effective, as his daughter

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.080
Hope's teddy bear is no longer being stained
with ash and blood.

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:06.280
Realizing Deadpool's sacrifice has saved his
daughter's life, he decides to pay the good

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:09.130
deed forward with a sacrifice of his own.

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:13.091
Cable uses the second of two time jumps his
machine is capable of to go back and make

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.640
sure that Deadpool's lead skee-ball token
ends up back in his pocket.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:21.720
Afterwards, the previous fight scene plays
out precisely as before, allowing Deadpool

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.179
to take the shot without his healing factor
active and still survive unharmed, the bullet

00:01:26.179 --> 00:01:29.530
deflected by the token instead of piercing
his heart.

00:01:29.530 --> 00:01:32.300
"Tell me they got that in slow motion."

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.280
Time to change

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:39.119
The first chunk of the post-credits sequence
opens up a massive can of worms, giving Deadpool

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:42.869
nothing less than the power to rewrite reality
as we know it.

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:47.490
Along with her girlfriend Yukio, Negasonic
Teenage Warhead alters Cable's time travel

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:52.240
device so it can make unlimited trips, turning
the machine from a limited-use, last resort

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.300
option into a glowing "I win" button.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.960
It's the worst possible power to endow a psycho
like Deadpool with, which N.T.W. seems to

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:03.130
only realize after she's handed the device
over to him.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.560
Just like that, Deadpool is off on his very
own excellent adventure.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.880
Unwasting Vanessa

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:13.330
Long before the wide release of Deadpool 2,
there was a swirl of negative buzz surrounding

00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:18.120
one of the movie's test screenings, part of
which had to do with Vanessa being "wasted".

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:21.710
It's pretty cheeky wording in retrospect,
once you know she gets shot through the chest

00:02:21.710 --> 00:02:23.180
in the movie's first act.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.040
It's not played for a joke, either.

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:29.500
The overblown opening credits sequence of
the movie, scored to Celine Dion's "Ashes",

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:32.140
highlights how impactful Vanessa's demise
is.

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:36.439
It's all the more satisfying when Deadpool
uses the time machine to go back to the scene

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:40.140
of her death and bisect her assassin's brain
with a cream cheese spreader.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.000
It's an insanely violent way to get to a happy
ending, but it's a happy ending we'll take.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.080
Searching for Sugar Bear

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:51.510
The second task Deadpool embarks on after
saving the love of his life is travelling

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.400
through time to save the true love of the
audience - Rob Delaney's Peter.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:59.080
After surviving the high-risk, high-altitude
parachute jump like a regular member of the

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:04.520
Army Rangers, Peter is ready to go all-out
on the heroism by saving the life of Zeitgeist,

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.720
he of the useless vomiting power.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:11.540
The first time around, this selfless act resulted
in Peter violently dissolving thanks to a

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.780
spray of Zeitgeist's acid bile.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.209
When Deadpool comes back to the moment via
the time machine, he sends Peter away from

00:03:17.209 --> 00:03:22.250
Zeitgeist's crash site emphatically, letting
X-Force's most vulnerable member live to fight

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:22.900
another day.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.700
X-Men Origins: Redux

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:30.560
With his second turn at the time machine,
Deadpool goes back to either the 2009 of our

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:35.780
world or the late seventies of the X-Men's
world to intercept the climax of X-Men Origins:

00:03:35.780 --> 00:03:36.300
Wolverine.

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:41.520
That movie infamously ended with Hugh Jackman's
Wolverine having a nonsensical duel with Ryan

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:45.420
Reynolds' proto-Deadpool, who you might remember
as the Merc with No Mouth.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:49.970
The real Deadpool finally corrects the timeline
in Deadpool 2, capping his old self eight

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:52.380
or nine times while Jackman's Wolverine looks
on.

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.280
Widely-distributed masochism

00:03:55.820 --> 00:04:00.019
There's something very Canadian about the
way Ryan Reynolds continually apologizes for

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.100
his past mistakes.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:05.760
In the third portion of Deadpool 2's end credits
world tour, the actor Ryan Reynolds excitedly

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.940
reads the script for Warner Bros. Green Lantern
movie, sometime in 2010.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.780
But this time, Reynolds' life comes to an
end before he gets the chance to make the

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.060
misbegotten movie, his blood and brain matter
being sprayed across the page as Deadpool

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:18.580
shoots him.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:23.780
It's the bloodiest, goriest, strangest mea
culpa the world has ever seen in a superhero

00:04:23.780 --> 00:04:27.640
movie, and the new Exhibit A in what makes
these movies so magical.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:30.060
Aaaaaand cut

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:34.720
One thing that's bound to bug some fans is
the fact that Deadpool 2 apparently filmed,

00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:38.860
and then cut, a scene in which Deadpool goes
back in time to smother Baby Hitler in his

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:39.380
crib.

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.700
Originally, the last stop on Wade Wilson's
Excellent Time Travel Tour was somewhere in

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:45.680
Austria in the year 1889.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:50.250
There, Deadpool proceeded to do something
we all might not be brave enough to do, given

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:50.880
the chance.

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:55.800
It's arguably the most heroic thing anyone's
ever done in a superhero movie, but did it

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:56.960
go too far?

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.220
Well, someone thought so.

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:02.800
According to a Comicbook.com interview with
Rhett Reese and Paul Wernick, two of the movie's

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:07.190
depraved screenwriters, the scene was cut
because the implications were just too uncomfortable

00:05:07.190 --> 00:05:08.240
to end the movie on.

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:11.440
"I think it was cut just because it was at
the very, very end.

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:16.720
And it left the audience with this, 'oooh,
sure it was Baby Hitler, but it IS a baby!"

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:18.600
The next episode

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:23.700
While the final shots of the film's main story
seem to suggest more adventures on the horizon,

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:27.180
it's possible that those adventures won't
be solo missions anymore.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.780
Like Weasel says in the Deadpool trailer,
they probably won't even make a Three.

00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:31.880
"Yeah, why would they?

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.320
You stop at Two — you killed it."

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:38.640
The idea that the main Deadpool series may
be done isn't just conjecture, either - it's

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.420
actually something Ryan Reynolds has come
out and said.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.700
Speaking to Entertainment Weekly, Reynolds
stated,

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:45.580
"I don't know that there would be a Deadpool
3.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:46.849
I really don't."

00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:51.070
Instead, Reynolds envisions Deadpool's future
as being one of a larger team, or half of

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:51.740
a partnership.

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:56.580
Granted, those are just where his thoughts
are as of the end of an exhausting movie production.

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:58.490
We imagine he's just being cautious.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:02.110
In case watching him get his brains blown
out over the script of Green Lantern didn't

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:06.410
make it clear, he's clearly tired of doing
lousy superhero movies, and that's a good

00:06:06.410 --> 00:06:07.410
thing for viewers.

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:10.720
Whether on a team or on his own, Deadpool's
future looks bright.

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:12.360
Thanks for watching!

00:06:12.380 --> 00:06:14.340
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:16.580
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

